  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I am well aware of a post that's already talking about instantiating GameObjects/Prefabs that contain UdonBehaviours, however I have dug a bit deeper to understand the cause.\n\nEssentially what's causing the crash is the PhotonView ID being duplicated and I assume trying to replace its self.\nYou can notice this error if you add the Prefab to the scene and try to instantiate while using the debug logger. I attached an image showing the log error.\nI noticed that you can still call methods, get variables, etc within the Prefab after you instantiate it by getting its class using the following.\n\n'ClassName variable = (ClassName)prefabObject.GetComponent(typeof(UdonBehaviour))'\n\nHowever I have noticed that some events such as Collisions (in my case) will be the death of the script whenever they occur.\nA way to get around this bug (at least somewhat) is to have the prefab in the scene (nest it in an empty or something), set its active to false, then in your instantiation method for that prefab, set its active to true after you have instantiated it. You can even do it within the prefab if you call a method within it's behavior class.\n\nAdditional reference to the bug can be found here: https://feedback.vrchat.com/vrchat-udon-closed-alpha-bugs/p/587-instantiated-prefabs-dont-have-udon-behaviours-when-in-vrc-not-editor\n\n- SDK3 2020.11.30.20.04\n- UdonSharp v0.18.8",
